{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01U9qYMGdWieYyjvfTsfrHgA","type":"tool_result","content":"3890\t        \"Cloudflare Turnstile free tier supports unlimited domains and verifications\",\n3891\t        \"Reference: https://developers.cloudflare.com/turnstile/\"\n3892\t      ],\n3893\t      \"dependencies\": [],\n3894\t      \"estimatedComplexity\": \"small\",\n3895\t      \"passes\": true\n3896\t    },\n3897\t    {\n3898\t      \"id\": \"US-173\",\n3899\t      \"title\": \"Implement A/B testing with Vercel Feature Flags and Edge Config\",\n3900\t      \"priority\": \"medium\",\n3901\t      \"description\": \"Set up Vercel Feature Flags using Edge Config to run server-side A/B tests on the /book page hero CTA and room card layouts without client-side flicker or layout shift. Edge Config reads are under 1ms p99 globally, making flags safe to evaluate in Next.js Middleware. Start with a CTA copy test to measure booking conversion impact scientifically.\",\n3902\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n3903\t        \"Vercel Edge Config store created and connected to the project\",\n3904\t        \"@vercel/edge-config and @vercel/flags packages installed\",\n3905\t        \"A/B flag defined for /book page primary CTA copy (e.g., 'Book Now' vs 'Check Availability' vs 'Get Best Price Direct')\",\n3906\t        \"Flag evaluated in Next.js Middleware and variant cookie set before page render — zero layout shift\",\n3907\t        \"GA4 custom dimension records which variant each session received for statistical analysis\",\n3908\t        \"Vercel Flags UI in dashboard shows flag status, rollout percentage, and per-user override capability\"\n3909\t      ],\n3910\t      \"technicalNotes\": [\n3911\t        \"Install: npm install @vercel/edge-config @vercel/flags\",\n3912\t        \"Read flag in middleware.ts: import { get } from '@vercel/edge-config'; const variant = await get('cta-variant')\",\n3913\t        \"Pass variant via x-variant response header or cookie to Server Component for conditional rendering\",\n3914\t        \"Flags as Code pattern: define flag types in flags.ts, resolve server-side only to prevent client exposure\",\n3915\t        \"Reference: https://vercel.com/docs/feature-flags, https://vercel.com/docs/edge-config\"\n3916\t      ],\n3917\t      \"dependencies\": [],\n3918\t      \"estimatedComplexity\": \"medium\",\n3919\t      \"passes\": false,\n3920\t      \"model\": \"haiku\",\n3921\t      \"_skipped\": true,\n3922\t      \"_skipReason\": \"Consistently oversized diff (12854 lines, limit 500)\",\n3923\t      \"_scopeCreep\": true,\n3924\t      \"last_attempted\": \"2026-04-14T06:17:59Z\"\n3925\t    },\n3926\t    {\n3927\t      \"id\": \"US-174\",\n3928\t      \"title\": \"Add complete favicon and Apple Touch Icon set for all platforms\",\n3929\t      \"priority\": \"medium\",\n3930\t      \"description\": \"Generate and deploy a full icon set covering all modern platforms: Apple Touch Icon (180×180 for iOS home screen), Android maskable icon (512×512 with safe zone), Windows tile icon (270×270), and an SVG favicon for modern browsers. Without a proper Apple Touch Icon, iOS users adding the site to their home screen see a generic screenshot rather than a branded icon, reducing PWA discoverability.\",\n3931\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n3932\t        \"<link rel='apple-touch-icon' sizes='180x180' href='/apple-touch-icon.png'> present in layout <head>\",\n3933\t        \"Web app manifest references icon entries for 192×192 (standard) and 512×512 (maskable purpose) PNG\",\n3934\t        \"SVG favicon at /favicon.svg with <link rel='icon' type='image/svg+xml' href='/favicon.svg'>\",\n3935\t        \"ICO fallback favicon.ico present in public/ for legacy browser support\",\n3936\t        \"Apple Touch Icon has no transparent background (iOS renders white on transparent — use solid background)\",\n3937\t        \"Maskable icon has main content within 80% safe area for Android adaptive icon cropping\",\n3938\t        \"All icons use the hostel's brand colours and are recognisable at 16×16px\"\n3939\t      ],\n3940\t      \"technicalNotes\": [\n3941\t        \"Generate icon set from a 512×512 source using realfavicongenerator.net or sharp.js\",\n3942\t        \"In Next.js App Router: place favicon.ico and apple-touch-icon.png in the app/ directory for auto-detection\",\n3943\t        \"Or use Next.js metadata API: export const metadata = { icons: { apple: '/apple-touch-icon.png', icon: [{ url: '/favicon.svg', type: 'image/svg+xml' }] } }\",\n3944\t        \"Reference: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Manifest/icons\"\n3945\t      ],\n3946\t      \"dependencies\": [],\n3947\t      \"estimatedComplexity\": \"small\",\n3948\t      \"passes\": true\n3949\t    },\n3950\t    {\n3951\t      \"id\": \"US-175\",\n3952\t      \"title\": \"Add WhatsApp Business Platform Cloud API for booking confirmation notifications\",\n3953\t      \"priority\": \"medium\",\n3954\t      \"description\": \"Integrate the WhatsApp Business Platform (Cloud API) to send automated template messages to guests after inquiry submission or deposit payment. Unlike the existing wa.me deep-link (outbound only), this enables programmatic outbound notifications: guests receive a WhatsApp message with booking confirmation, check-in instructions, and hostel location link. First 1,000 business-initiated conversations per month are free.\",\n3955\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n3956\t        \"Meta for Developers app configured with WhatsApp Business Cloud API and a verified business phone number\",\n3957\t        \"POST /api/whatsapp-notify Route Handler sends an approved WhatsApp template message after contact form submission\",\n3958\t        \"Template message includes: guest name, booking reference (or inquiry ID), hostel address, and check-in contact link\",\n3959\t        \"Template registered and approved in Meta Business Manager before any sending\",\n3960\t        \"WHATSAPP_TOKEN and WHATSAPP_PHONE_NUMBER_ID stored as Vercel environment variables\",\n3961\t        \"GET /api/whatsapp-webhook handles Meta's hub.challenge verification handshake\"\n3962\t      ],\n3963\t      \"technicalNotes\": [\n3964\t        \"Cloud API send message endpoint: POST https://graph.facebook.com/v21.0/{phone_number_id}/messages\",\n3965\t        \"Required body: { messaging_product: 'whatsapp', to: '+60XXXXXXXXXX', type: 'template', template: { name: 'booking_confirmation', language: { code: 'en' }, components: [...] } }\",\n3966\t        \"Free tier: first 1,000 business-initiated conversations per month; subsequent conversations ~$0.0735 USD per conversation (MY pricing)\",\n3967\t        \"Webhook GET verification: respond with parseInt(hub.challenge) when hub.verify_token === WHATSAPP_WEBHOOK_VERIFY_TOKEN\",\n3968\t        \"Reference: https://developers.facebook.com/docs/whatsapp/cloud-api/get-started\"\n3969\t      ],\n3970\t      \"dependencies\": [],\n3971\t      \"estimatedComplexity\": \"large\",\n3972\t      \"passes\": false,\n3973\t      \"model\": \"haiku\",\n3974\t      \"_skipped\": true,\n3975\t      \"_skipReason\": \"Requires WhatsApp Business Platform Cloud API credentials — not implementable in this codebase\"\n3976\t    },\n3977\t    {\n3978\t      \"id\": \"US-176\",\n3979\t      \"title\": \"Automate structured data validation in CI with schema.org validator\",\n3980\t      \"priority\": \"medium\",\n3981\t      \"description\": \"Add a CI step that validates all JSON-LD structured data against schema.org schemas before production deploy, catching type errors, missing required properties, and invalid enum values before they reach Google's crawlers. Currently structured data is written manually and only verified ad-hoc via Google Rich Results Test — a CI check prevents silent regressions when schema files are edited.\",\n3982\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n3983\t        \"CI step runs structured data validation as part of the GitHub Actions build workflow\",\n3984\t        \"Validation covers: LodgingBusiness, BlogPosting, FAQPage, BreadcrumbList, HowTo, and Event schema types\",\n3985\t        \"Build fails if any JSON-LD block contains schema.org type errors, unknown properties, or missing required fields\",\n3986\t        \"Validation output is reported in GitHub Actions summary with page URL, schema type, and specific error for each violation\",\n3987\t        \"CI step runs on push to main and on all PRs that modify any StructuredData component or schema data file\"\n3988\t      ],\n3989\t      \"technicalNotes\": [\n3990\t        \"Use 'structured-data-testing-tool' npm package for offline validation without external API calls: npm install -D structured-data-testing-tool\",\n3991\t        \"Run: npx sdtt --url https://staging-url.vercel.app --schema LodgingBusiness --schema BlogPosting\",\n3992\t        \"Alternative for local validation: use 'schema-dts' TypeScript types to catch type errors at compile time\",\n3993\t        \"For post-deploy validation, the Google Search Console URL Inspection API can be called from CI to check live pages\",\n3994\t        \"Reference: https://developers.google.com/search/docs/appearance/structured-data\"\n3995\t      ],\n3996\t      \"dependencies\": [],\n3997\t      \"estimatedComplexity\": \"medium\",\n3998\t      \"passes\": false,\n3999\t      \"model\": \"sonnet\",\n4000\t      \"_skipped\": true,\n4001\t      \"_skipReason\": \"Requires external CI setup for schema.org validator — not frontend code\"\n4002\t    },\n4003\t    {\n4004\t      \"id\": \"US-177\",\n4005\t      \"title\": \"Add JSON Feed 1.1 at /feed.json for blog content syndication\",\n4006\t      \"priority\": \"low\",\n4007\t      \"description\": \"Expose a /feed.json endpoint following JSON Feed v1.1 specification as a modern JSON alternative to the existing RSS/Atom feeds. JSON Feed is natively consumable by JavaScript apps, AI agents, and modern feed readers without XML parsing overhead. Enables hostel blog content (JB travel tips, events, promotions) to be syndicated to modern platforms and aggregators.\",\n4008\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n4009\t        \"GET /feed.json returns 200 with Content-Type: application/feed+json\",\n4010\t        \"Response includes required fields: version (https://jsonfeed.org/version/1.1), title, items array\",\n4011\t        \"Each item includes: id, url, title, content_html, date_published, authors array, and language\",\n4012\t        \"Top-level language field set to 'en' with per-item override for Malay/Chinese content if applicable\",\n4013\t        \"<link rel='alternate' type='application/feed+json' title='Pelangi Blog' href='/feed.json'> added to layout <head>\",\n4014\t        \"Feed includes all published blog posts newest-first with full content_html\"\n4015\t      ],\n4016\t      \"technicalNotes\": [\n4017\t        \"Implement as Next.js Route Handler at app/feed.json/route.ts\",\n4018\t        \"Return NextResponse with headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/feed+json; charset=utf-8' }\",\n4019\t        \"Reuse blog post data source from existing blog TypeScript data files\",\n4020\t        \"JSON Feed 1.1 spec: https://www.jsonfeed.org/2020/08/07/json-feed-version.html\",\n4021\t        \"Coexists with existing RSS at /feed.xml — both can be present simultaneously\"\n4022\t      ],\n4023\t      \"dependencies\": [],\n4024\t      \"estimatedComplexity\": \"small\",\n4025\t      \"passes\": true\n4026\t    },\n4027\t    {\n4028\t      \"id\": \"US-178\",\n4029\t      \"title\": \"Add CSS print stylesheet for booking confirmation and receipt pages\",\n4030\t      \"priority\": \"low\",\n4031\t      \"description\": \"Add @media print CSS rules to the booking confirmation and /book pages so guests can print or save-as-PDF a clean, readable booking record. Without print styles, navigation, cookie banners, chat widgets, and booking CTAs clutter the printed output, making the page unusable as a physical or PDF booking reference that guests may need for customs, visa applications, or accommodation proof.\",\n4032\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n4033\t        \"@media print CSS hides navigation, footer, cookie banner, chat widget, sticky booking bar, and all CTAs\",\n4034\t        \"Booking reference number, dates, room type, price, and hostel full address/contact details are clearly visible when printed\",\n4035\t        \"All text renders in black (#000) on white (#fff) in print mode — no coloured backgrounds consume ink\",\n4036\t        \"Body font size is at least 12pt for readability on A4 paper\",\n4037\t        \"Page breaks are avoided within booking summary blocks using page-break-inside: avoid\",\n4038\t        \"Print preview in Chrome shows a clean, professional 1-page booking confirmation\"\n4039\t      ],\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5db64454-1df5-4c1c-9e81-ebba85b5ca40","uuid":"cc22088d-0b23-48db-a862-2c5e1bf66d30","timestamp":"2026-04-14T06:18:50.825Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\prd.json","content":"        \"Cloudflare Turnstile free tier supports unlimited domains and verifications\",\n        \"Reference: https://developers.cloudflare.com/turnstile/\"\n      ],\n      \"dependencies\": [],\n      \"estimatedComplexity\": \"small\",\n      \"passes\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-173\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement A/B testing with Vercel Feature Flags and Edge Config\",\n      \"priority\": \"medium\",\n      \"description\": \"Set up Vercel Feature Flags using Edge Config to run server-side A/B tests on the /book page hero CTA and room card layouts without client-side flicker or layout shift. Edge Config reads are under 1ms p99 globally, making flags safe to evaluate in Next.js Middleware. Start with a CTA copy test to measure booking conversion impact scientifically.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Vercel Edge Config store created and connected to the project\",\n        \"@vercel/edge-config and @vercel/flags packages installed\",\n        \"A/B flag defined for /book page primary CTA copy (e.g., 'Book Now' vs 'Check Availability' vs 'Get Best Price Direct')\",\n        \"Flag evaluated in Next.js Middleware and variant cookie set before page render — zero layout shift\",\n        \"GA4 custom dimension records which variant each session received for statistical analysis\",\n        \"Vercel Flags UI in dashboard shows flag status, rollout percentage, and per-user override capability\"\n      ],\n      \"technicalNotes\": [\n        \"Install: npm install @vercel/edge-config @vercel/flags\",\n        \"Read flag in middleware.ts: import { get } from '@vercel/edge-config'; const variant = await get('cta-variant')\",\n        \"Pass variant via x-variant response header or cookie to Server Component for conditional rendering\",\n        \"Flags as Code pattern: define flag types in flags.ts, resolve server-side only to prevent client exposure\",\n        \"Reference: https://vercel.com/docs/feature-flags, https://vercel.com/docs/edge-config\"\n      ],\n      \"dependencies\": [],\n      \"estimatedComplexity\": \"medium\",\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"model\": \"haiku\",\n      \"_skipped\": true,\n      \"_skipReason\": \"Consistently oversized diff (12854 lines, limit 500)\",\n      \"_scopeCreep\": true,\n      \"last_attempted\": \"2026-04-14T06:17:59Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-174\",\n      \"title\": \"Add complete favicon and Apple Touch Icon set for all platforms\",\n      \"priority\": \"medium\",\n      \"description\": \"Generate and deploy a full icon set covering all modern platforms: Apple Touch Icon (180×180 for iOS home screen), Android maskable icon (512×512 with safe zone), Windows tile icon (270×270), and an SVG favicon for modern browsers. Without a proper Apple Touch Icon, iOS users adding the site to their home screen see a generic screenshot rather than a branded icon, reducing PWA discoverability.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"<link rel='apple-touch-icon' sizes='180x180' href='/apple-touch-icon.png'> present in layout <head>\",\n        \"Web app manifest references icon entries for 192×192 (standard) and 512×512 (maskable purpose) PNG\",\n        \"SVG favicon at /favicon.svg with <link rel='icon' type='image/svg+xml' href='/favicon.svg'>\",\n        \"ICO fallback favicon.ico present in public/ for legacy browser support\",\n        \"Apple Touch Icon has no transparent background (iOS renders white on transparent — use solid background)\",\n        \"Maskable icon has main content within 80% safe area for Android adaptive icon cropping\",\n        \"All icons use the hostel's brand colours and are recognisable at 16×16px\"\n      ],\n      \"technicalNotes\": [\n        \"Generate icon set from a 512×512 source using realfavicongenerator.net or sharp.js\",\n        \"In Next.js App Router: place favicon.ico and apple-touch-icon.png in the app/ directory for auto-detection\",\n        \"Or use Next.js metadata API: export const metadata = { icons: { apple: '/apple-touch-icon.png', icon: [{ url: '/favicon.svg', type: 'image/svg+xml' }] } }\",\n        \"Reference: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Manifest/icons\"\n      ],\n      \"dependencies\": [],\n      \"estimatedComplexity\": \"small\",\n      \"passes\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-175\",\n      \"title\": \"Add WhatsApp Business Platform Cloud API for booking confirmation notifications\",\n      \"priority\": \"medium\",\n      \"description\": \"Integrate the WhatsApp Business Platform (Cloud API) to send automated template messages to guests after inquiry submission or deposit payment. Unlike the existing wa.me deep-link (outbound only), this enables programmatic outbound notifications: guests receive a WhatsApp message with booking confirmation, check-in instructions, and hostel location link. First 1,000 business-initiated conversations per month are free.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Meta for Developers app configured with WhatsApp Business Cloud API and a verified business phone number\",\n        \"POST /api/whatsapp-notify Route Handler sends an approved WhatsApp template message after contact form submission\",\n        \"Template message includes: guest name, booking reference (or inquiry ID), hostel address, and check-in contact link\",\n        \"Template registered and approved in Meta Business Manager before any sending\",\n        \"WHATSAPP_TOKEN and WHATSAPP_PHONE_NUMBER_ID stored as Vercel environment variables\",\n        \"GET /api/whatsapp-webhook handles Meta's hub.challenge verification handshake\"\n      ],\n      \"technicalNotes\": [\n        \"Cloud API send message endpoint: POST https://graph.facebook.com/v21.0/{phone_number_id}/messages\",\n        \"Required body: { messaging_product: 'whatsapp', to: '+60XXXXXXXXXX', type: 'template', template: { name: 'booking_confirmation', language: { code: 'en' }, components: [...] } }\",\n        \"Free tier: first 1,000 business-initiated conversations per month; subsequent conversations ~$0.0735 USD per conversation (MY pricing)\",\n        \"Webhook GET verification: respond with parseInt(hub.challenge) when hub.verify_token === WHATSAPP_WEBHOOK_VERIFY_TOKEN\",\n        \"Reference: https://developers.facebook.com/docs/whatsapp/cloud-api/get-started\"\n      ],\n      \"dependencies\": [],\n      \"estimatedComplexity\": \"large\",\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"model\": \"haiku\",\n      \"_skipped\": true,\n      \"_skipReason\": \"Requires WhatsApp Business Platform Cloud API credentials — not implementable in this codebase\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-176\",\n      \"title\": \"Automate structured data validation in CI with schema.org validator\",\n      \"priority\": \"medium\",\n      \"description\": \"Add a CI step that validates all JSON-LD structured data against schema.org schemas before production deploy, catching type errors, missing required properties, and invalid enum values before they reach Google's crawlers. Currently structured data is written manually and only verified ad-hoc via Google Rich Results Test — a CI check prevents silent regressions when schema files are edited.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"CI step runs structured data validation as part of the GitHub Actions build workflow\",\n        \"Validation covers: LodgingBusiness, BlogPosting, FAQPage, BreadcrumbList, HowTo, and Event schema types\",\n        \"Build fails if any JSON-LD block contains schema.org type errors, unknown properties, or missing required fields\",\n        \"Validation output is reported in GitHub Actions summary with page URL, schema type, and specific error for each violation\",\n        \"CI step runs on push to main and on all PRs that modify any StructuredData component or schema data file\"\n      ],\n      \"technicalNotes\": [\n        \"Use 'structured-data-testing-tool' npm package for offline validation without external API calls: npm install -D structured-data-testing-tool\",\n        \"Run: npx sdtt --url https://staging-url.vercel.app --schema LodgingBusiness --schema BlogPosting\",\n        \"Alternative for local validation: use 'schema-dts' TypeScript types to catch type errors at compile time\",\n        \"For post-deploy validation, the Google Search Console URL Inspection API can be called from CI to check live pages\",\n        \"Reference: https://developers.google.com/search/docs/appearance/structured-data\"\n      ],\n      \"dependencies\": [],\n      \"estimatedComplexity\": \"medium\",\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"model\": \"sonnet\",\n      \"_skipped\": true,\n      \"_skipReason\": \"Requires external CI setup for schema.org validator — not frontend code\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-177\",\n      \"title\": \"Add JSON Feed 1.1 at /feed.json for blog content syndication\",\n      \"priority\": \"low\",\n      \"description\": \"Expose a /feed.json endpoint following JSON Feed v1.1 specification as a modern JSON alternative to the existing RSS/Atom feeds. JSON Feed is natively consumable by JavaScript apps, AI agents, and modern feed readers without XML parsing overhead. Enables hostel blog content (JB travel tips, events, promotions) to be syndicated to modern platforms and aggregators.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"GET /feed.json returns 200 with Content-Type: application/feed+json\",\n        \"Response includes required fields: version (https://jsonfeed.org/version/1.1), title, items array\",\n        \"Each item includes: id, url, title, content_html, date_published, authors array, and language\",\n        \"Top-level language field set to 'en' with per-item override for Malay/Chinese content if applicable\",\n        \"<link rel='alternate' type='application/feed+json' title='Pelangi Blog' href='/feed.json'> added to layout <head>\",\n        \"Feed includes all published blog posts newest-first with full content_html\"\n      ],\n      \"technicalNotes\": [\n        \"Implement as Next.js Route Handler at app/feed.json/route.ts\",\n        \"Return NextResponse with headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/feed+json; charset=utf-8' }\",\n        \"Reuse blog post data source from existing blog TypeScript data files\",\n        \"JSON Feed 1.1 spec: https://www.jsonfeed.org/2020/08/07/json-feed-version.html\",\n        \"Coexists with existing RSS at /feed.xml — both can be present simultaneously\"\n      ],\n      \"dependencies\": [],\n      \"estimatedComplexity\": \"small\",\n      \"passes\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-178\",\n      \"title\": \"Add CSS print stylesheet for booking confirmation and receipt pages\",\n      \"priority\": \"low\",\n      \"description\": \"Add @media print CSS rules to the booking confirmation and /book pages so guests can print or save-as-PDF a clean, readable booking record. Without print styles, navigation, cookie banners, chat widgets, and booking CTAs clutter the printed output, making the page unusable as a physical or PDF booking reference that guests may need for customs, visa applications, or accommodation proof.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"@media print CSS hides navigation, footer, cookie banner, chat widget, sticky booking bar, and all CTAs\",\n        \"Booking reference number, dates, room type, price, and hostel full address/contact details are clearly visible when printed\",\n        \"All text renders in black (#000) on white (#fff) in print mode — no coloured backgrounds consume ink\",\n        \"Body font size is at least 12pt for readability on A4 paper\",\n        \"Page breaks are avoided within booking summary blocks using page-break-inside: avoid\",\n        \"Print preview in Chrome shows a clean, professional 1-page booking confirmation\"\n      ],","numLines":150,"startLine":3890,"totalLines":5537}}}
